The little town was quiet in the early morning. The sun was low, the air was cool, and the streets were almost empty. A small cat sat near the old stone wall and watched the birds move between the trees.

The cat liked the garden behind the house. Every morning, it walked through the grass, stopped near the flowers, and waited. Sometimes a bird landed nearby. Sometimes a leaf moved in the wind. Sometimes nothing happened at all.

Across the road, a baker opened his shop. He placed fresh bread on the wooden shelves and opened the front door. The smell of warm bread slowly filled the street. People began to arrive, one by one.

A man bought bread and coffee. A woman bought bread and cheese. A child looked through the window and asked for a small cake.

The baker smiled and said, "Good morning."

The child smiled and said, "Good morning."

The cat heard the voices from across the road, but it stayed in the garden.

Later, the sun moved higher in the sky. The quiet street became busy. Cars passed, people talked, doors opened, and doors closed. The baker continued working.

In the afternoon, the street became quiet again. The cat returned to the stone wall. The birds returned to the trees. The wind moved through the leaves.

The day was simple, but the same small patterns appeared again and again.

The cat walked.
The bird flew.
The wind moved.
The baker worked.
The people talked.

The cat walked through the garden.
The cat walked near the wall.
The cat walked across the grass.

The bird flew over the house.
The bird flew over the garden.
The bird flew into the tree.

The wind moved the leaves.
The wind moved the grass.
The wind moved through the trees.

Morning became afternoon, and afternoon became evening. The shops closed, the people went home, and the street became quiet once more.

The cat sat near the old stone wall and watched the empty road.
